# THE CHANGELOG IS NOT MERGED WITH `union`, AND THE REASON IS MEASURED.
#
# It was, from the day the contract was written, on this reasoning: the file is
# append-at-the-top, so two branches that each ship an entry insert at the same
# line and collide every time; union keeps BOTH insertions instead of raising a
# conflict, and the stamper then assigns the numbers.
#
# The stated hazard was "two branches editing the SAME EXISTING entry", called
# rare, and the everyday prepend was called safe. That is backwards. **The
# prepend is the case that corrupts**, because union is a LINE union and an
# entry is not a line: when both sides prepend, the shared closing `    ] },`
# is common context and survives ONCE, so the first entry swallows the second
# and the literal is left with an unclosed bracket. The result is still valid
# JavaScript — `node --check` passes it — so nothing downstream notices until a
# human reads the file.
#
# Measured 2026-08-15: this happened on FIVE consecutive merges in one day
# (#126, #132, #136, #139, R-BUG4), each needing the same manual repair —
# rebuild from the base copy and re-stamp. Union did not save one conflict; it
# converted five loud conflicts into five silent corruptions that had to be
# repaired by hand anyway.
#
# So the changelog merges normally now. Two branches that both ship an entry
# CONFLICT, loudly, at the moment of the merge, and the resolution is the
# obvious one: keep both entries, newest first, and re-run
# `node chicago/4d/tools/stamp-changelog.mjs`.
#
# The old comment also claimed "the contract check catches that — versions must
# be strictly decreasing". That check DOES exist (`check-changelog.mjs`, the
# `entries must be newest-first by v` rule) and always has. What it could not do
# is REPORT: it lives after the module load, and the shape walk above it calls
# report() and exits the moment a bracket is unbalanced. The merge that creates
# a duplicate version is the same merge that breaks the shape, so the run always
# died on the shape first and the duplicate was never named — then the hand
# repair rebuilt the file from a base copy, taking the duplicate with it. The
# check was right and unreachable in exactly the case it was written for.
# It is now ALSO enforced in the text scan, which runs before that exit, so a
# duplicate is reported even when the literal will not load.
#
# See polecat-platform docs/SHELL-API.md § the fleet changelog contract. The
# fleet's other apps carry the same `merge=union` line and the same exposure.
